9,51838,109362,52035,109393,52233,109424,52430,109454,52628,109483,52826,109511,53024,109538,53222,109565,53420,109591,53618,109616,53817,109641,54015,109664,54214,109687,54412,109709,54611,109730,54810,109750,55009,109770,55208,109789,55407,109807,55606,109824,55805,109840,56005,109856,56204,109870,56404,109884,56603,109898,56803,109910,57002,109922,57202,109932,57402,109942,57601,109952,57801,109960,58001,109968,58201,109974,58400,109980,58600,109986,58800,109990,59000,109994,59200,109996,59400,109998,59600,110000,59800]}],"gcode":"","notes":"INLAY COASTER\nA round coaster with an eight-point star inlaid in it.\n\nOperations\n1. Inlay pocket: the star is V-carved into the coaster, 4 mm deep, with the 60° V-bit; the flat end mill clears the floor.\n2. Inlay plug: the matching star, cut from a separate piece of darker wood (6 mm). It is cut a little smaller (0.05 mm) so it presses in, and the V-bit gives it the sloped sides that fit the pocket.\n3. Profile (outside): cuts the coaster out, leaving 4 small holding tabs.\n\nAssembly\n- Cut the pocket first, then put the dark piece on the machine and cut the plug (the G-code is split into one file per piece).\n- Glue the plug into the pocket, let it dry, then sand the face flat: the plug stands a little proud on purpose.\n- Cut the coaster out last, so the stock stays held while you work on the face.\n\nBefore cutting for real\n- Set X0 Y0 at the lower-left corner and Z0 on the top of the stock, and tick \"Air cut\" in each operation for a first run.","act":3,"oid":3}}